anchors:
  - TinyRustLM.com owns browser-local chat and its current clean-slate product contracts.
  - TinyRustLM.MiRust.com owns current developer and architecture documentation.
  - MiniModel.org owns catalog/discovery and authorized initial current-model seeding; server model downloads do not authorize remote inference or prompt upload.
  - MiniModel.MiRust.com owns MiniModel developer/protocol documentation.
  - MiRust.com owns ecosystem architecture, evidence, research, and governance documentation.
  - MemoryEndpoints.com supports direct ecosystem agent coordination and the separate TinyRustLM.com Connect user long-term-memory plugin.
  - Local UAIX files and approved private stores remain valid synchronized prelaunch resilience copies.
  - No talisman or memory file creates runtime enforcement, credentials, deployment authority, model quality, live service proof, or campaign progress.

ownership_review:
  reports: R10, R15
  runtime: Current Rust runtime and browser integration live in TinyRustLM.com; do not relocate ownership to Runtime.MiRust.com because a report assumes its name defines its role.
  retired_brand: Runtime.MiRust.com is retired as a separate public documentation authority; SLMComposer.com is not the canonical app identity.
  composer: LMComposer.com is the actual discovered repository name. Its remaining implementation role requires inspection; do not equate it with every historical Composer brand.
  contracts: Each boundary needs one inspected owner, exact current schema, identities, bounds, errors, cancellation and success evidence. No duplicate implementations or documentation mirrors.
